From: cod3 port
Subject: [PATCH] xam: keep the launch path XamLoaderLaunchTitle builds

XamLoaderLaunchTitle joins a bare name ("default.xex") to the running
program's folder, but held the result in a std::string_view (auto from
MappedPtr<char>::value()), which pointed at the joined temporary only until
the end of that statement. The launch path then started with whatever the
allocator wrote into the freed buffer (16 bytes on glibc), e.g.
"<garbage>0\Partition1\default.xex" in cod3mp's log when its reboot
command starts the campaign. A std::string keeps it.
---
diff --git a/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp b/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp
--- a/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp
+++ b/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp
@@ -268,7 +268,9 @@
 
   // Translate the launch path to a full path.
   if (raw_name_ptr) {
-    auto path = raw_name_ptr.value();
+    // A copy: path takes the joined string below, which a string_view
+    // would only point at until the end of that statement.
+    std::string path(raw_name_ptr.value());
     if (path.empty()) {
       loader_data.launch_path = "game:\\default.xex";
     } else {
